Package: phylogp
Title: Phylogenetic Comparative Models as Gaussian Processes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Thomas A.", "Püschel", , "thomas.puschel@anthro.ox.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits phylogenetic comparative models for continuous traits as
    Gaussian processes on a tree. Models are built by adding kernels
    (Brownian motion, Pagel's lambda, kappa and delta, early burst,
    Ornstein-Uhlenbeck, relaxed rates, rate through time, distance-based
    kernels and user-defined branch-wise kernels). The package writes the
    corresponding 'Stan' program, uses a linear-time pruning likelihood
    whenever the kernel has a branch-wise form, and computes leave-one-out
    predictive densities in linear time. Tools check whether a kernel is a
    valid covariance on a given tree and plot the correlations it implies.
